{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And enmity, etc.</b> The Judge judges the law of the blood-avenger, for since all the seed of the woman caused him death, the blood-avenger pursues and strikes the killer — and this is what it says, <b>he shall bruise your head</b>: meaning, what you did to him at the beginning, for he opened with evil. Or it may say ״head״ on account of the head, upon which life depends, and there is the slaughter of the angel of death. <b>And you shall bruise him, the heel</b> — because in the end he was drawn from those upon whom came all the curses. Or it may say <b>heel</b>, because his heels were cut off and he goes on his belly." "<b>And if</b> you would say: Granted, saying <b>he shall bruise your head</b> makes sense, for a person's heart burns over what the serpent did, and he would kill it. But what the serpent received from the curses is punishment for what it had already done — so what place is there to bruise the heel? The reason is that the serpent has a retort in its mouth: she should not have listened to its words, for between the words of the teacher and the words of the student, whose are heard? (Sanhedrin 29a) — and no harm would have been drawn, neither to him nor to her. You thus learn that she is the one who encircled, and from the aspect of this claim he would have enmity against her. And it hinted at the time of each one's attainment of victory, saying <b>he shall bruise you</b> when he is <b>head</b> — meaning, when he magnifies his worth and exalts himself in the aspect of Torah and commandments; <b>and you shall bruise him</b> when he is <b>heel</b> in decline. And so it is: all the while that Israel do the will of the Place, the serpent bends its head, and the reverse, Heaven forfend. Further, it alludes to the deed of Rabbi Chanina ben Dosa (Berakhot 33a), whom a serpent bit in his foot and the serpent died — and according to this, he bruised it with his foot against the serpent's head."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:50.619745315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}